# {{projectName}} - Project Knowledge Base

## Project Overview
This is a **NestJS** application built with TypeScript that provides {{#if isGraphQL}}a **GraphQL API**{{/if}}{{#if isRest}}a **REST API**{{/if}} using {{#if isMongoose}}**MongoDB** with **Mongoose**{{/if}}{{#if isPrisma}}**{{#if_eq database 'postgresql'}}PostgreSQL{{/if_eq}}{{#if_eq database 'mysql'}}MySQL{{/if_eq}}** with **Prisma**{{/if}} as the database layer.

### Technology Stack
- **Framework**: NestJS with TypeScript
- **API Type**: {{#if isGraphQL}}GraphQL (Apollo Server){{/if}}{{#if isRest}}REST API with Swagger documentation{{/if}}
- **Database**: {{#if isMongoose}}MongoDB with Mongoose ODM{{/if}}{{#if isPrisma}}{{#if_eq database 'postgresql'}}PostgreSQL{{/if_eq}}{{#if_eq database 'mysql'}}MySQL{{/if_eq}} with Prisma ORM{{/if}}
{{#if hasRedis}}- **Caching**: Redis{{/if}}
{{#if hasElasticsearch}}- **Search**: Elasticsearch{{/if}}
{{#if hasRabbitmq}}- **Messaging**: RabbitMQ{{/if}}

## Architecture Principles

### Module Organization
Each feature is organized as a self-contained module with the following structure:

```
src/entity/
├── entity.module.ts              # Module definition and dependencies
{{#if isGraphQL}}├── entity.resolver.ts           # GraphQL resolver (queries/mutations){{/if}}
{{#if isRest}}├── entity.controller.ts        # REST controller (HTTP endpoints){{/if}}
├── entity.service.ts             # Business logic layer
{{#if isMongoose}}├── entity.repository.ts        # Data access layer
├── entity.schema.ts              # MongoDB schema definition{{/if}}
{{#if isGraphQL}}├── inputs/                      # GraphQL input types
│   ├── entity-create.input.ts
│   ├── entity-update.input.ts
│   └── entity-find-many.input.ts
├── objects/                      # GraphQL object types
│   └── entity.object.ts{{/if}}
{{#if isRest}}├── dto/                         # REST data transfer objects
│   ├── create-entity.dto.ts
│   ├── update-entity.dto.ts
│   └── entity-response.dto.ts{{/if}}
└── errors/                       # Custom error definitions
    ├── entity.errors.ts
    └── entity-not-found.error.ts
```

### Dependency Flow
The application follows a layered architecture:
```
{{#if isGraphQL}}GraphQL Resolvers{{/if}}{{#if isRest}}REST Controllers{{/if}} → Services{{#if isMongoose}} → Repositories → Mongoose Models{{/if}}{{#if isPrisma}} → PrismaService{{/if}}
```

## Coding Standards and Patterns

### File Naming Conventions
- **Modules**: `entity.module.ts`
- **Services**: `entity.service.ts`
{{#if isGraphQL}}- **Resolvers**: `entity.resolver.ts`
- **GraphQL Objects**: `entity.object.ts`
- **GraphQL Inputs**: `entity-operation.input.ts`{{/if}}
{{#if isRest}}- **Controllers**: `entity.controller.ts`
- **DTOs**: `entity-operation.dto.ts`{{/if}}
{{#if isMongoose}}- **Repositories**: `entity.repository.ts`
- **Schemas**: `entity.schema.ts`{{/if}}
- **Errors**: `entity-specific.error.ts`

{{#if isGraphQL}}
### GraphQL Conventions

#### Resolver Naming
- **Queries**: `entity` (single), `entities` (multiple)
- **Mutations**: `entityCreate`, `entityUpdate`, `entityDelete`

#### Argument Constants
Always use these constants from `src/common/common.constraints.ts`:
```typescript
const INPUT_KEY = 'input';
const INPUT_PAGINATION = 'pagination'; 
const INPUT_SORT = 'sort';
```

#### Resolver Method Pattern
```typescript
@Query(() => EntityObject)
async entity(@Args(INPUT_KEY) input: EntityInput): Promise<EntityObject> {
  return this.entityService.findById(input.id);
}

@Query(() => EntityPaginationResponse)
async entities(
  @Args(INPUT_KEY) input: EntityFindManyInput,
  @Args(INPUT_SORT) sort: EntitySortInput,
  @Args(INPUT_PAGINATION) pagination: PaginationInput,
): Promise<EntityPaginationResponse> {
  return this.entityService.findAll(input, sort, pagination);
}
```

#### GraphQL Object Constructor Pattern
{{#if isMongoose}}For MongoDB documents, always use this constructor pattern:
```typescript
@ObjectType()
export class EntityObject {
  constructor(input: EntityDocument | EntityObject) {
    Object.assign(this, {
      ...((input as any)._doc
        ? (input as EntityDocument).toObject({ virtuals: true })
        : input),
    });
  }

  @Field(() => ID)
  id: string;

  @Field()
  name: string;
}
```{{/if}}
{{#if isPrisma}}For Prisma entities:
```typescript
@ObjectType()
export class EntityObject {
  @Field(() => ID)
  id: string;

  @Field()
  name: string;

  constructor(entity: Entity) {
    Object.assign(this, entity);
  }
}
```{{/if}}
{{/if}}

{{#if isRest}}
### REST API Conventions

#### Controller Pattern
```typescript
@Controller('entities')
@ApiTags('entities')
export class EntityController {
  constructor(private readonly entityService: EntityService) {}

  @Get()
  @ApiOperation({ summary: 'Retrieve all entities' })
  @ApiResponse({ status: 200, type: [EntityResponseDto] })
  async findAll(): Promise<EntityResponseDto[]> {
    return this.entityService.findAll();
  }

  @Post()
  @ApiOperation({ summary: 'Create a new entity' })
  @ApiResponse({ status: 201, type: EntityResponseDto })
  async create(@Body() dto: CreateEntityDto): Promise<EntityResponseDto> {
    return this.entityService.create(dto);
  }
}
```

#### DTO Validation Pattern
```typescript
export class CreateEntityDto {
  @ApiProperty({ description: 'Entity name', example: 'Example Entity' })
  @IsString()
  @MinLength(2)
  @MaxLength(100)
  name: string;
}
```
{{/if}}

### Error Handling System

#### Base Error Classes
Located in `src/common/errors/business.error.ts`:
- `BusinessError` - General business logic errors
- `ValidationError` - Input validation errors  
- `AuthenticationError` - Authentication failures
- `NotFoundError` - Resource not found
- `ForbiddenError` - Access denied
- `InternalError` - System errors

#### Custom Error Pattern
Always extend base errors, never use them directly:
```typescript
export const ENTITY_NOT_FOUND_CODE = 'ENTITY_NOT_FOUND';

export class EntityNotFoundError extends NotFoundError {
  constructor() {
    super('Entity not found', ENTITY_NOT_FOUND_CODE);
  }
}
```

{{#if isGraphQL}}#### Error Registration
Register error codes in `src/utils/registerEnums.ts`:
```typescript
export const Errors = {
  ...GqlCommonErrors,
  ...GqlEntityErrors,
};
```{{/if}}

{{#if isMongoose}}
### MongoDB/Mongoose Patterns

#### Schema Definition
```typescript
@Schema()
export class Entity {
  @Prop({ required: true, unique: true })
  name: string;

  @Prop({ default: Date.now })
  createdAt: Date;

  @Prop({ default: Date.now })
  updatedAt: Date;
}

export type EntityDocument = Entity & Document;
export const EntitySchema = SchemaFactory.createForClass(Entity);
```

#### Repository Pattern
```typescript
@Injectable()
export class EntityRepository {
  constructor(
    @InjectModel(Entity.name) 
    private readonly entityModel: Model<EntityDocument>,
  ) {}

  async findById(id: string): Promise<EntityDocument | null> {
    return this.entityModel.findById(id).exec();
  }

  async create(data: Partial<Entity>): Promise<EntityDocument> {
    const entity = new this.entityModel(data);
    return entity.save();
  }
}
```

#### Schema Registration
Always register schemas in `src/common/modules/app-mongoose-models.module.ts`:
```typescript
@Module({
  imports: [
    MongooseModule.forFeature([
      { name: Entity.name, schema: EntitySchema },
    ]),
  ],
  exports: [MongooseModule],
})
export class AppMongooseModelsModule {}
```
{{/if}}

{{#if isPrisma}}
### Prisma Patterns

#### Service with Prisma
```typescript
@Injectable()
export class EntityService {
  constructor(private readonly prisma: PrismaService) {}

  async findById(id: string): Promise<Entity | null> {
    return this.prisma.entity.findUnique({
      where: { id },
    });
  }

  async create(data: Prisma.EntityCreateInput): Promise<Entity> {
    return this.prisma.entity.create({
      data,
    });
  }

  async update(id: string, data: Prisma.EntityUpdateInput): Promise<Entity> {
    return this.prisma.entity.update({
      where: { id },
      data,
    });
  }
}
```

#### Transaction Pattern
```typescript
async createWithProfile(entityData: any, profileData: any): Promise<Entity> {
  return this.prisma.$transaction(async (tx) => {
    const entity = await tx.entity.create({ data: entityData });
    await tx.profile.create({ 
      data: { ...profileData, entityId: entity.id } 
    });
    return entity;
  });
}
```
{{/if}}

